From ca48f84e879cfaa0fd0799993d4520d6776c1a77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotlouis <1891109+dotlouis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:21:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 39/41] MTROPOLIS: Draw elements at the size scripts give them

Scripts resize elements to shrink or grow their pictures, but the
contents were always drawn at their original size:

- Setting the size of a Thereware Rotator now scales the drawing from
  the element's top left corner, by the ratio to the size the element
  had when the size was first used.
- An mToon element authored at the size of its mToon is stretched when
  a script resizes it. Elements authored at another size (where the
  size only sets the clickable area) are still drawn unscaled. Clones
  keep the authored size.
- With a Rotator, an mToon is centered in its element, which is as
  large as the bounds of the rotated mToon, like images are.
- Transformed drawings are clipped to the window themselves, since
  transBlitFrom stretched them into the clipped area.

Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage shrinks the objects put in the album
margin into their small frames this way; they were drawn full size,
off their frames.

